From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 23:33:15 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: Give the VPU power domain its
 supply

BUCK4 feeds the VPU rail but nothing on this board says so. The vendor
kernel's regulator_summary lists the VPU power domain and the VPU itself
against BUCK4, and BUCK3 against the GPU domain, so describe the second
half of that pair the same way as the first.

No functional change today: BUCK4 is marked regulator-always-on, so
unlike BUCK3 it was never at risk of being switched off as unused. This
is for completeness, and so the domain rather than a constraint keeps
the rail up.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index f8bd1e4..8c27fbe 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -263,6 +263,10 @@
 	power-supply = <&buck3>;
 };
 
+&pgc_vpu {
+	power-supply = <&buck4>;
+};
+
 &fec1 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_fec1>;
